{"term":"debate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d5b2219078c372e2a3","definition":"To participate in a debate; to dispute, argue, especially in a public arena.","example":"\"Debate me, coward!\" snarled the completely normal intellectual.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["contend","canvass"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, reciprocal","register":"ambitransitive, reciprocal","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:41ea27ae5c968b5c5c","definition":"To fight.","example":"Well knew they both his person, sith of late / With him in bloudie armes they rashly did debate.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, reciprocal","register":"intransitive, obsolete, reciprocal","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e26987b216b1ba88c6","definition":"To engage in combat for; to strive for.","example":"Volunteers […] thronged to serve under his banner, and the cause of religion was debated with the same ardour in Spain as on the plains of Palestine.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:133b34c4d95ed86335","definition":"To consider (to oneself), to think over, to attempt to decide","example":"He was debating where he'd spend his holiday.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:009a19d7ed35ba6db1","definition":"An argument, or discussion, usually in an ordered or formal setting, often with more than two people, generally ending with a vote or other decision.","example":"After a four-hour debate, the committee voted to table the motion.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating","antidebate","balloon debate","debate bro","debateful","Debategate","debatelord","debatey","make-debate","metadebate","nondebate","postdebate","predebate","pseudodebate","self-debate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6098f3197529f9b2da","definition":"An informal and spirited but generally civil discussion of opposing views.","example":"The debate over the age of the universe is thousands of years old.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["debatability","debatable","debater","debatingly","mass debate","outdebate","redebate","undebating","antidebate","balloon debate","debate bro","debateful","Debategate","debatelord","debatey","make-debate","metadebate","nondebate","postdebate","predebate","pseudodebate","self-debate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Ka